Package: Atlas
Title: Automated Model Building with LLM Agents
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Matt", "O'Reilly", email = "fermoymatt@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds statistical and machine learning models by driving an
    agentic large language model loop via 'ellmer'. The agent explores the
    data, proposes a modelling plan for user approval, then writes and runs R
    code to fit, compare, and refine candidate models. Domain knowledge can
    be supplied as machine-verified constraints (mandatory variables,
    monotone effects, custom checks), every step is checkpointed to disk so
    sessions survive interruption and can be resumed, and the complete code
    trail is returned for reproducibility. Data never leaves the local R
    session; the model only sees column metadata and printed summaries.
